Z||000001||fix||10-05-2001||07:54 PM||||Mine came off easy with just a little bumping with a rubber mallet.  If you haven't tried that, just give it a few whacks.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||normalicy||10-05-2001||07:58 PM||||I had no difficulties.  You sure that you got all the bolts?  If my memory is correct, there are 6 bolts.  2 top, 2 middle, 2 lower.  The gravity of the engine was enough to loosen itself.<P>------------------<BR>What is normal anyway?||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||10-05-2001||09:13 PM||||grrdoublepost!<p>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 10-05-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000004||artherd||10-05-2001||09:13 PM||||Don't forget the *&$#@(&$#*( dust-sheild!!! (damn thing is on there with more bolts than hold the tranny...)<P>Sometimes you'll have to drop the starter.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000005||Bazooka||10-05-2001||09:41 PM||||Elenor84,<BR>   First you shoud have removed the Flywheel Attaching Bolts that are accessible after removing the dust shield (at the bottom rear of the engine). Once those are out (and any tranny lines from automatics) the BellHousing to Engine Bolts can be removed and the Tranny should fall away from the engine. <BR>****************************<BR>Originally posted by Elenor84:<BR>[B]Hey guys...I removed all thebolts and yada yada yada...now hwo do I "pry" it off?  What tool do I use?  thx!<BR>*****************************<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Bazooka (edited 10-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Eric_PA||10-05-2001||10:50 PM||||If you have an automatic, don't forget the flywheel bolts holding on the torque converter. Also the dust shield. Other than that they practically fall off.<P>Eric<p>[This message has been edited by Eric_PA (edited 10-05-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000007||Elenor84||10-06-2001||03:44 AM||||Ok I didn't remove the bolts where the starter goes in...that sheild that surrounds it...so if I remove those she should come out?<BR>and there was 2 on top and 2 on each side but I couldn't see any underneith...were are they?<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Bazooka||10-06-2001||03:41 PM||||Lance,<BR>Remove the dust shield thats underneath the center of the flywheel. Once that is off, you can see some of the attaching bolts for the Flywheel to Torque Converter. Also you will haave to rotate the engine by hand to see the upper hidden bolts on the Flywheel. Use a socket on the front Crankshaft Dampener to rotate the flywheel by hand about 1/3 of the way at a time. Reinstalling the engine and tranny is done the same way. <BR>****************************<BR>Originally posted by Elenor84:<BR>[B]Ok I didn't remove the bolts where the starter goes in...that sheild that surrounds it...so if I remove those she should come out?<BR>and there was 2 on top and 2 on each side but I couldn't see any underneith...were are they?<BR>*************************************<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Bazooka (edited 10-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Elenor84||10-06-2001||05:00 PM||||Thx bazooka...I'll go give that a try!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||roadwarrior||10-06-2001||09:55 PM||||pry it off with a screw driver, just be very careful not to damage the tranny housing. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Elenor84||10-06-2001||10:02 PM||||Ok guys I"m getting really frustrated here...there  was 5 big main bolts I took out then there was a bolt going threw the tranny and then to the engine...all this one had was a nut on it and I removed it...is that the 6?<BR>If not were the heck is the 6th bolt?  there was 2 on top...then 2 more on each side...plus one more on the left side(looking from left side of engine strait at tranny)but were is the 6th one?  I looked all over...there isn't one...but the bloody tranny still won't come off...I pounded on it with a malet but it only moved a couple of milimeters...then nothing...any more advice?<BR>O ya and I did remove the sheild from the fly wheel but no more bolts were reveiled at all....I have a 4 speed and its from a 86SE...<P><BR>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg">  </A><p>[This message has been edited by Elenor84 (edited 10-06-2001).]||||reg||1
