Z||000016||Bazooka||10-07-2001||12:30 PM||||Lance,    It sounds like you just about have it loose. Go back underneath where you removed the dust shield. Look at the flywheel with the teeth on its ring gear. Now look on the surface of the Flywheel. There should be 1 or 2 Bolt Heads visible on the surface of the lower portion of the flywheel. Remove them. Then go to the front of the engine and turn the Crank Dampener Bolt (Harmonic Balancer) about 1/3 of the way around. Then go back to the Flywheel and loosen any other Bolts that you can reach from the dust shield opening. You will have to rotate the crank Dampener Bolt another 1/3 of a rotation before you'lle have access to the last bolts that secure the Torque Converter to the Flywheel inside the bell housing. Naturally, the axles should be removed and finally, the attachment bolts to the engine (outside).<BR>Good Luck<BR>************************<BR>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Elenor84:<BR><B>O ya and I did remove the sheild from the fly wheel but no more bolts were reveiled at all....I have a 4 speed and its from a 86SE...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>************************<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Bazooka (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Rodrv6||10-07-2001||02:28 PM||||Ummmm---<BR>There are no flywheel bolts to remove on the manual transmission.  Only the automatic has torque convertor bolts that need to be removed.  If all the transmission to engine block bolts are out, then the transmission should pull off the back and out of the clutch.  There are a couple of locating pins pressed into the engine that can be difficult to release.  If there is a small gap all the way around the mating surface, then you probably just need to gently pry the two apart.  It will take about 3/8" before the locating pins will be free from the transmission and then it should be free.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Rodrv6 (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||Gerald||10-07-2001||09:12 PM||||Lance, I just finished my clutch today. Pain in the ass but I did it if I remember correctly you have a manual, right? I don't quite know what your saying but e-mail me and tell me where you live and Ill come take a look at it for ya if you want.||||reg||1
